    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "i get the algorithm stuff but that feels like a way to dodge the question. people in the movement aren't just posting random videos, they're talking about deep systemic corruption and things that have actually been happening. if you look past the \"misinformation\" label that the media uses, what are the specific core grievances or realities they are pointing to that actually have merit?",
